  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction**: NF_db improves by ~0.6 dB.  \n*Rationale*: The primary failure is due to poor noise matching and high input-referred noise. The gate of NM1 (n2) is floating except through resistors, leading to a high impedance node that is sensitive to noise and instability. Adding C5 (a capacitor from n2 to VSS) creates a low-impedance AC ground at the gate, which stabilizes the gate voltage and reduces gate noise. This is a standard technique in LNA design: bypassing the gate to ground at RF reduces the effective noise contribution from the input transistor. This directly improves the noise figure by reducing the input-referred thermal noise and improving matching.",
